   "l": "By this the sage's governing: he empties their hearts,\nfills their bellies,",
   "v": true,
   "i": "So the sage governs by emptying their hearts and filling their bellies,",
   "n": "虛 'empty' and 實 'solid, full' are adjectives doing duty as verbs, and causative verbs at that: 'make empty', 'make full'. This is the part-of-speech fluidity of chapter 1 taken one step further, and the next unit does it twice more. 其 'their' has no antecedent but 民 'the people' above. Do not read the emptying as cruelty: the heart in this text is the seat of scheming and craving rather than of feeling, and it is set deliberately against the belly, which is what actually keeps a person alive."
