   "l": "weakens their wills,\nstrengthens their bones.",
   "v": true,
   "i": "weakening their wills and strengthening their bones.",
   "n": "The same causative adjectives: 弱 'weak' becomes 'weaken', 強 'strong' becomes 'strengthen'. 強 has to be chosen — qiáng is 'strong', qiǎng is 'to force' — and the parallel with 弱 fixes it as qiáng. The four objects are paired on purpose: heart against belly, will against bone. What schemes and wants is thinned out; what carries a person is filled and made firm."
